  <metadata>
    <name>Blue Ridge Parkway</name>
    <desc>Blue Ridge Parkway - Complete route from Rockfish Gap, VA (Milepost 0, near Waynesboro/Afton) to Cherokee, NC (Milepost 469). 469 miles of scenic mountain road through the Blue Ridge Mountains of Virginia and North Carolina. One of the most popular cycling routes in the eastern United States, with approximately 49,000 feet of total elevation gain. The parkway connects Shenandoah National Park in Virginia to Great Smoky Mountains National Park in North Carolina, reaching a maximum elevation of 6,047 feet at Richland Balsam (Milepost 431).</desc>
    <author>
      <name>OpenStreetMap Contributors</name>
      <link href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/relation/55450">
        <text>OSM Relation 55450</text>
      </link>
    </author>
